/-!
# Actual cohomology equivalences induced by the sphere map

The original continuous sphere map induces native integral cohomology
equivalences in every degree. The forward maps are its original pullbacks,
the constructed inverses preserve the native evaluation pairing, and both
directions preserve the original Alexander--Whitney cup products.

This is a statement about the actual induced maps, not a homotopy equivalence
or a smooth recognition theorem.
-/
